# Agent workflow

## Before editing

- Confirm product scope, assumptions, tradeoffs, and verifiable success criteria.
- Inspect nearby code, tests, scripts, and rules before introducing a pattern.
- Identify security, configuration, subprocess, file-system, and extension/webview boundary risks.
- Decide whether tests, documentation, or rule updates are required.

## Before finalizing

- Satisfy the request without unrelated cleanup.
- Add or update tests when behavior changed.
- Run focused verification first, then broaden when shared behavior changed.
- Document new commands, settings, configuration, and user-facing behavior.
- Keep `.claude/rules/` (canonical), matching `.cursor/rules/`, and `AGENTS.md` synchronized when policy changes.

## Commit messages

- Write an English `type(topic): Subject` line, then a blank line and a Korean body carrying `[Issue]`, `[Problem]`, `[Cause & Measure]`, and `[Checking Method]` in that order.
- Keep the subject at 50 characters or less with no trailing period; `(topic)` is optional.
- Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `test`, `refactor`, `style`, `chore`.
- Write `N/A` for a label the change does not support, and never invent a verification result.
- End with `Signed-off-by: Maroomir Yoon <maroomir@gmail.com>`. Do not add `Co-Authored-By` trailers.

## Final report

Summarize changed files, implemented behavior, relevant security/configuration notes, verification results or limitations, rule updates, and remaining follow-up work.
